From: Salah Ahmed <haddad2inc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath79: ar8216: skip PHYs on another switch's internal MDIO bus

CONFIG_AR8216_PHY is built into every ath79 kernel on the generic
subtarget and its phy_driver matches the PHY IDs of the QCA83xx port PHYs
(0x004d0000/0xffff0000 covers 0x004dd036), so it also probes the PHYs that
qca8k exposes on the switch's internal MDIO bus once a board is converted
to DSA.

That is fatal on ath79: 730-ar8216-make-reg-access-atomic.patch wraps every
register access in local_irq_save()/local_irq_restore() and warns that it
"breaks the driver on any mdio master with interrupts used". qca8k's MDIO
master takes a mutex, may allocate and transmit skbs
(qca8k_phy_eth_command) and busy-waits up to QCA8K_BUSY_WAIT_TIMEOUT
(2000 ms) per transaction, while ar8xxx_read_id() retries up to
AR8X16_PROBE_RETRIES times. On a single-core MIPS this locks the CPU up
with interrupts disabled, the watchdog keepalive starves and the board
resets in a loop before preinit.

Skip PHYs whose MDIO bus is parented by an mdio_device that is not bound
to this driver: that is another switch's internal bus. SoC MDIO buses
(ag71xx, mdio-gpio, mdio-bitbang) are parented by platform devices, and our
own ar8xxx-mdio bus is exempted by comparing the parent's driver, so
swconfig boards - including the built-in switches described by the
"mdio-bus" child node in qca956x.dtsi, qca953x.dtsi, ar7240.dtsi and
ar9330.dtsi - are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Salah Ahmed <haddad2inc@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/ar8216.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/ar8216.c
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
 #include "ar8216.h"
+
+
+/* defined at the bottom of this file; used to recognise our own bus */
+static struct mdio_driver ar8xxx_mdio_driver;
 
 extern const struct ar8xxx_chip ar8327_chip;
 extern const struct ar8xxx_chip ar8337_chip;
@@ -2605,6 +2609,27 @@
 	if (phydev->mdio.addr != 0 && phydev->mdio.addr != 3 && phydev->mdio.addr != 4)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
+	/*
+	 * Never claim a PHY that lives on another switch driver's internal
+	 * MDIO bus, such as the one qca8k registers for the QCA83xx port
+	 * PHYs. The register accessors below disable interrupts around every
+	 * transaction (730-ar8216-make-reg-access-atomic.patch), which is only
+	 * safe for the polling-mode MDIO masters used on ath79: qca8k's MDIO
+	 * master takes a mutex, may allocate and transmit skbs and busy-waits
+	 * up to 2000 ms per access, so probing through it with interrupts off
+	 * locks the CPU up and starves the watchdog.
+	 *
+	 * Such a bus is parented by an mdio_device; SoC MDIO buses (ag71xx,
+	 * mdio-gpio, mdio-bitbang) are parented by platform devices instead.
+	 * Our own ar8xxx-mdio bus is also parented by an mdio_device, so it is
+	 * exempted by comparing the parent's driver.
+	 */
+	if (phydev->mdio.bus->parent &&
+	    phydev->mdio.bus->parent->bus == &mdio_bus_type &&
+	    phydev->mdio.bus->parent->driver !=
+	        &ar8xxx_mdio_driver.mdiodrv.driver)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	if (!ar8xxx_is_possible(phydev->mdio.bus))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
